{
"dur": 61.531,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 7.839,
"text": "The officers go to check the number plate, and the fake couple simply drive off in the stolen car. Round the corner, he asks why she did it.",
"end": 8.114
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 8.114,
"vo_start": 8.389,
"vo_end": 18.144,
"text": "It's for her mum, she says. Her mum wants to be an estate agent, and in that game you have to look rich. Then they swap names. Jason. Lucia.",
"end": 18.419
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 18.419,
"vo_start": 18.694,
"vo_end": 30.333,
"text": "The game jumps ahead. They're living together now, and Lucia notices that Jason goes out on jobs and comes home with bundles of cash. She wants in. He says no: this life isn't for you.",
"end": 30.608
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 30.608,
"vo_start": 30.883,
"vo_end": 39.563,
"text": "Fine, she says, I'll do it on my own. Hard cut. A recorded voice: this is a call from an inmate at Hamlet Correctional. Lucia is in prison.",
"end": 39.838
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 39.838,
"vo_start": 40.113,
"vo_end": 50.232,
"text": "How did she get there? She was in a caf\u00e9 with no money, told the staff her purse was in the car, walked next door and held up a payday-loan shop. It went badly wrong.",
"end": 50.507
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 50.507,
"vo_start": 50.782,
"vo_end": 60.581,
"text": "She actually escaped. Then she went back, and got caught. Because what she'd left in that caf\u00e9 wasn't a purse. It was her baby son, Tom\u00e1s.",
"end": 61.531
}
],
